# THE LAST ACCEPTED FLOW G1 BASELINE: the scheduler's transition rows,
# <platform> <row> <total ns> <count> <toolchain> — one machine's, so the
# gate compares like with like. Written by `sh tools/flow_bench/run.sh
# --record`; held by `make flow-gate`. No row on a machine, no gate there.
#
# `c_gate_round_trip` is the empty-ready-queue transition; `c_spawn_one`
# crosses it twice a task; `c_spawn_parked_cold` crosses it cold and
# carries the stack guard's own first-touch cost. These rows are the
# runtime before that transition cost was added (77fc7b1~1), recorded on
# a Sprite (the checks' image): the line a runtime PR must hold.
linux-x86_64 c_gate_round_trip 15169967 200000 Ubuntu clang version 22.1.2 (1ubuntu1)
linux-x86_64 c_spawn_one 1866041 10000 Ubuntu clang version 22.1.2 (1ubuntu1)
linux-x86_64 c_spawn_parked_cold 85660451 10000 Ubuntu clang version 22.1.2 (1ubuntu1)
